== 1. WHAT THE EARLY EXIT COSTS vs WHAT ROUTING IT THROUGH `run()` COSTS
   Option 1 says to remove the early exit and let the drift path fall through to
   `run()`. `run()` is three `bend` processes, so that is the price of the refusal.
   Bounded, and the VERDICT TOKEN is parsed rather than the exit status -- rc 3 is a
   memory kill and rc 1 is a refusal, and both are non-zero.
   the refusal (drift, pin dead)  [bounded] WITHIN-LIMITS  rc=2  peak-RSS=0 MB (ceiling 2048)  0s  :: /Users/cyberistic/src/tries/2026-09-30-tinybendygrad/.venv/bin/python /Users/cyberistic/src/tries/2026-09-30-tinybendygrad/.agents/slop/clearfix/variants/NOW-mixin-op-gate-drift.py  out=0B err=263B  said=ORACLE DRIFT: .agents/slop/mixinop/oracle-op-gate.sh: e8792d0ff1ad9d1a != pinned 178cf5f74e923c4a | the frozen shell oracle moved, so this run would compare against nothing. Restore it, or re-freeze it deliberately and update ORACLE_PIN -- do not delete the pin.
   a GREEN run of the same gate   [bounded] WITHIN-LIMITS  rc=0  peak-RSS=1728 MB (ceiling 2048)  10s  :: /Users/cyberistic/src/tries/2026-09-30-tinybendygrad/.venv/bin/python /Users/cyberistic/src/tries/2026-09-30-tinybendygrad/.agents/slop/clearfix/variants/NOW-mixin-op-gate-green.py  out=107B err=0B
   And bmn, whose measured peak is 1,531 MB against a 2,048 MB ceiling and which the
   brief records as a coin flip at that ceiling: routing a 2 MB refusal through three
   `bend` processes to LEARN the pin moved is not a safety improvement, it is a new
   way to be killed. Option 1 is therefore rejected on cost, not on taste.

